apitrace: --skip-draws=N, replay frames before N without their draw calls

Benchmarking one frame of a long trace means replaying every frame before
it to rebuild the state it starts from, and drawing them is the one part
of that the measured frame does not need: their pixels are overwritten.
--skip-draws=N skips the draw calls of frames before N and runs the rest -
state, uploads, display-list calls (a list can change state), immediate
mode (an unpaired glBegin would derail the stream), and any draw issued
between glNewList and glEndList, which records into the list rather than
drawing. Applies on top of apitrace-headless.patch.

